    "Recorded on the Python and platform named in oracle.environment; the CI platform (Linux, Node 22.x and 24.x for the checks) was not exercised for the oracle.",
    "Releases under pins.not_covered exist but were not exercised; no claim is made for them or for any version other than the pins.",
    "Nothing here ran against a database server or an application: the oracle configures settings with an empty DATABASES, calls django.setup() and reads model _meta, it runs no migration, no query and no manage.py command, so status.runtime_tested stays false.",
    "The migration scanner reads Flyway and Liquibase layouts only (see probes.migration_plane); Django makemigrations was not run.",
    "Every fixture is registered as the app \"shop\"; another app label changes the default table names. The provider is given each models.py as plain source text and reads classes that extend models.Model directly; abstract bases, inheritance, proxy and swappable models are not compared.",
    "The drift comparator reports one direction per call; both calls are recorded. expected_changes is the set difference of two oracle snapshots, not the output of makemigrations, and a column with the same name but a different type is not seen.",
    "Only SQL-visible constructs are compared (tables, columns, primary keys, foreign keys); defaults, indexes, unique and check constraints, validation, managers and signals are not. The oracle lists indexes, constraints and custom default managers as unmodeled tokens only."
